    "annotations": [
        {
            "id": "ann_1",
            "type": "note",
            "text": "ConvolutionTOP \u2014 Custom Kernel via Expressions\n\nPreset is set to 'Custom' (index 0), which starts as an identity kernel.\nThe Custom preset uses center=1.0, all others=0.0 (passthrough).\n\nTo build your own kernel, set individual kernel weights via expressions\non the ConvolutionTOP's internal kernel array. For example, this patch\nanimates the divisor to create a pulsing effect on the identity output.\n\nFor a full custom kernel, you would typically:\n1. Set preset=Custom, kernel_size=3\n2. Use spare parameters to expose the 9 kernel weights\n3. Wire expressions from those spares into the kernel\n\nThe built-in presets (Emboss, Sharpen, Edge Detect, etc.) are\nhard-coded 3x3 kernels embedded into the center of larger sizes.",
            "position": [
                50.0,
                -150.0
